        "original_id": "f9baa5ba-2aad-5d81-8628-d98827dc3db4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Wadleigh, Barbara Kopple, Cathy Caplan, Thomas Haneke, Lawrence Silk, Albert Finney, Diane Venora, Gregory Hines, Edward James Olmos\n- Films: Woodstock, American Dream, Wolfen\n- Events: Woodstock Festival\n- Places: Bethel, New York, Akron, Ohio\n\nFacts:\n- The Woodstock Festival took place in August 1969 near Bethel, New York.\n- Woodstock is a 1970 documentary film about the Woodstock Festival.\n- Michael Wadleigh was born on September 24, 1942 in Akron, Ohio.\n- Michael Wadleigh, also known as Michael Wadley, is an American film director and cinematographer renowned for the documentary film Woodstock.\n- Wolfen is a 1981 American crime horror film directed by Michael Wadleigh and starring Albert Finney, Diane Venora, Gregory Hines, and Edward James Olmos.\n- American Dream is a 1990 cinéma vérité documentary film directed by Barbara Kopple and co-directed by Cathy Caplan, Thomas Haneke, and Lawrence Silk.",
